## API contract

- `openapi.json` is the committed API contract. A test compares it with the running app{% if language == 'java' %} (the Testcontainers integration test, so Docker is required){% endif %}. After changing endpoints or models, regenerate it with `UPDATE_OPENAPI=1` (PowerShell: `$env:UPDATE_OPENAPI=1`) and the test command{% if language == 'python' %} (`uv run pytest tests/test_openapi.py`){% else %} (`./gradlew test`){% endif %}, review the diff and commit it with the change.
{%- if github_ci %}
- The `api-compat` CI job diffs `openapi.json` against the base branch with oasdiff. Error-level breaking changes (removed endpoints, new required fields, narrowed types) fail the PR unless they are declared: put `!` in the title (`feat(api)!: drop v1 orders`) and a line starting `BREAKING CHANGE: <what clients must do>` in the PR body. Prefer additive changes to the published contract; make a breaking change only when the user decides to.
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
